ASSIGN task category\n    END FUNCTION\nEND CLASS\n\nCLASS TaskManager\n    FUNCTION __init__()\n        INITIALIZE tasks as empty list\n        CALL load_tasks() to load saved tasks from file\n    END FUNCTION\n\n    FUNCTION add_task(title: str, description: str, deadline: str, priority: str, category: str)\n        CALCULATE task_id as length of tasks + 1\n        CREATE new_task as instance of Task using given parameters\n        APPEND new_task to tasks\n        CALL save_tasks()\n    END FUNCTION\n\n    FUNCTION edit_task(task_id: int, title: str, description: str, deadline: str, priority: str, category: str)\n        FOR EACH task IN tasks\n            IF task.id equals task_id\n                UPDATE task.title\n                UPDATE task.description\n                UPDATE task.deadline\n                UPDATE task.priority\n                UPDATE task.category\n                CALL save_tasks()\n                RETURN\n            ENDIF\n        ENDFOR\n    END FUNCTION\n\n    FUNCTION load_tasks()\n        IF tasks.json file exists\n            OPEN tasks.json AS file\n                LOAD tasks_data from the file\n                FOR EACH task IN tasks_data\n                    CREATE Task using task data and APPEND to tasks\n                ENDFOR\n            CLOSE file\n        ENDIF\n    END FUNCTION\n\n    FUNCTION save_tasks()\n        OPEN tasks.json AS file\n            DUMP tasks to the file in JSON format\n        CLOSE file\n    END FUNCTION\nEND CLASS\n```\n', '|Case|:**search_for_specific_tasks** (duplicate handled)\n```pseudocode\nCLASS TaskManager\n    FUNCTION search_tasks(query: str)\n        RETURN LIST OF tasks WHERE query is found in task.title (case-insensitive)\n    END FUNCTION\nEND CLASS\n```\n**Key Libraries:**\n- `json`: Used for easy serialization and deserialization of task data to/from `tasks.json`.\n- `tkinter`: Utilized for creating the GUI, allowing users to interact with functionalities like adding and searching for task